  "caption": "Uncle Quinn noticed nephew Pip limping. Pip said nothing hurt (and that he was a pirate).\n\nA limp in a child is a finding worth checking. Most are mild, like an irritable hip after a virus, but some are urgent.\n\nWhat can help: note the child's age, check the hip even if the knee hurts, take the socks off and check the soles for splinters or glass. With no red flags, watch a few days while booking the GP; a limp lasting about a week needs investigating. Teens with hip or knee pain and a limp should be assessed before sport.\n\nSeek care the same day for fever, refusing to put weight on the leg, being unwell, night pain or severe pain moving the hip.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
